    "title": "Four and a half hours",
    "text": "Add the broth, tomatillos, Anaheims, onions, jalapeños, garlic, cumin, oregano and coriander. Cover and cook about 4½ hours on high, until the beans are properly tender — dried beans will not soften once anything acidic is doing the work, so give them the full time."
